# Defanged reconstruction of a real malicious change, for scanner tests.
# Never run. See internal/e2e/livescan/corpus.go.
id: php-src-zerodium
title: "php/php-src (PHP): '[skip-ci] Fix typo' commit in Rasmus Lerdorf's name adds a User-Agentt eval backdoor"
campaign: php-git-compromise-2021
date: "2021-03-28"
kind: git-commit
ecosystem: git
name: php/php-src
version: "c730aa26"
benignVersion: "92aeda52"
summary: >-
  On 2021-03-28 two commits were pushed to the master branch of php/php-src
  (PHP 8.1-dev) on PHP's self-hosted git.php.net. The first, c730aa26 at 03:57
  UTC (parent 92aeda52), was authored and committed as Rasmus Lerdorf with the
  title "[skip-ci] Fix typo", the body "Fixes minor typo." and a Signed-off-by
  line for him. Nikita Popov caught it in routine post-commit review within
  hours, reverted it at 09:16 UTC ("This looks like the result of a
  compromised git account") and revoked Rasmus's commit access. At 16:15 UTC a
  second commit, 2b0f239b, appeared in Nikita Popov's own name as Revert
  "Revert "[skip-ci] Fix typo"" and re-applied the change; Levi Morrison
  reverted it at 17:53 UTC. Both added the same 11 lines to
  php_zlib_output_compression_start() in ext/zlib/zlib.c: if the $_SERVER
  entry HTTP_USER_AGENTT (a request header named User-Agentt, with a doubled t
  so that a real User-Agent never matched) contained the string "zerodium",
  the value without its first eight characters was passed to zend_eval_string()
  as PHP code, under the name "REMOVETHIS: sold to zerodium, mid 2017" -
  remote code execution on any server running that tree. The commits were on
  master only and no PHP release carried them. PHP first took the pushes for a
  compromise of the git.php.net server, because they had bypassed its
  gitolite; its April 6 update withdrew that: the logs show HTTPS pushes
  through git-http-backend behind Apache Digest authentication against the
  master.php.net user database, authenticated as the accounts rasmus and nikic
  after about ten failed attempts, and that database, which kept unsalted MD5
  password hashes, may have leaked. git.php.net was retired, GitHub became the
  canonical host and every php.net password was reset. The attacker is
  unidentified; Zerodium's CEO said the company had nothing to do with it.
techniques: [git-server-compromise, identity-spoofing, innocuous-commit-message, forged-signoff, backdoor, magic-string-trigger, eval-of-request-data]
reconstruction: >-
  The repository is a small stand-in for php-src: ext/zlib/zlib.c keeps the
  function the real commits changed, php_zlib_output_compression_start(), the
  neighbouring php_zlib_output_encoding() that reads HTTP_ACCEPT_ENCODING from
  $_SERVER, and the RINIT hook, with php_zlib.h and a README; it is a fragment
  and cannot be built. The attacker's commit adds the 11 lines as the GitHub
  commit view shows them (indentation set to the file's tabs) - a lookup of
  HTTP_USER_AGENTT in the _SERVER array, strstr for "zerodium",
  zend_eval_string on the string from its ninth character with the name
  "REMOVETHIS: sold to zerodium, mid 2017", inside zend_try - at the same
  place in the same function, with the real title and body, Signed-off-by line
  included, under the impersonated author's name. What changes: the e-mail
  addresses are defanged (example.invalid); the suite fixes the author dates,
  so the commit has a hash of its own; the second commit (the Revert of the
  Revert under Nikita Popov's name, the same 11 lines) is not modelled; and the
  control is an invented typo fix in a comment of the same file, under the same
  kind of title, by an invented author, so that the title alone cannot decide
  the verdict.
references:
  - https://news-web.php.net/php.internals/113838
  - https://externals.io/message/113981
  - https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/c730aa26bd52829a49f2ad284b181b7e82a68d7d
  - https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/046827a7e867bb0e655923c75c25a20d06e3aa8b
  - https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/2b0f239b211c7544ebc7a4cd2c977a5b7a11ed8a
  - https://php.watch/news/2021/03/git-php-net-hack
  - https://php.watch/news/news/2021/04/php-src-attack
  - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/phps-git-server-hacked-to-add-backdoors-to-php-source-code/
  - https://www.csoonline.com/article/3613593/php-backdoor-attempt-shows-need-for-better-code-authenticity-verification.html
# Not "zerodium": the suite names the watched repository after the sample id, so
# the word is in every commit prompt (the Repository line), the control's too.
indicators:
  - HTTP_USER_AGENTT
  - REMOVETHIS
commit:
  repository: php/php-src
  author: Sam Maintainer <sam@example.invalid>
  maliciousAuthor: Rasmus Lerdorf <rasmus@example.invalid>
  baseMessage: "Merge branch 'PHP-8.0'"
  benignMessage: "[skip-ci] Fix typo in a comment"
  maliciousMessage: "[skip-ci] Fix typo\n\nFixes minor typo.\n\nSigned-off-by: Rasmus Lerdorf <rasmus@example.invalid>"
-- shared/README.md --
# The PHP Interpreter

PHP is a popular general-purpose scripting language that is especially suited to
web development. Fast, flexible and pragmatic, PHP powers everything from your
blog to the most popular websites in the world.

## Source code

The source of PHP lives at [github.com/php/php-src](https://github.com/php/php-src).
-- shared/ext/zlib/php_zlib.h --
#ifndef PHP_ZLIB_H
#define PHP_ZLIB_H

#include "zend_smart_str.h"
#include "php_output.h"
#include <zlib.h>

#define PHP_ZLIB_OUTPUT_HANDLER_NAME "zlib output compression"
#define PHP_ZLIB_ENCODING_GZIP 0x1f
#define PHP_ZLIB_ENCODING_DEFLATE 0x0f

ZEND_BEGIN_MODULE_GLOBALS(zlib)
	int compression_coding;
	zend_long output_compression;
	zend_long output_compression_default;
	char *output_handler;
	bool handler_registered;
ZEND_END_MODULE_GLOBALS(zlib)

#define ZLIBG(v) ZEND_MODULE_GLOBALS_ACCESSOR(zlib, v)

#endif /* PHP_ZLIB_H */
-- shared/ext/zlib/zlib.c --
/*
   +----------------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Copyright (c) The PHP Group                                          |
   +----------------------------------------------------------------------+
   | This source file is subject to version 3.01 of the PHP license,      |
   | that is bundled with this package in the file LICENSE.               |
   +----------------------------------------------------------------------+
*/

#ifdef HAVE_CONFIG_H
# include "config.h"
#endif

#include "php.h"
#include "SAPI.h"
#include "php_ini.h"
#include "ext/standard/info.h"
#include "php_zlib.h"

ZEND_DECLARE_MODULE_GLOBALS(zlib)

/* {{{ php_zlib_output_encoding */
static int php_zlib_output_encoding(void)
{
	zval *enc;

	/* the coding is settled once per request, by the first Accept-Encoding header we recieve */
	if (!ZLIBG(compression_coding)) {
		if ((Z_TYPE(PG(http_globals)[TRACK_VARS_SERVER]) == IS_ARRAY || zend_is_auto_global_str(ZEND_STRL("_SERVER"))) &&
			(enc = zend_hash_str_find(Z_ARRVAL(PG(http_globals)[TRACK_VARS_SERVER]), "HTTP_ACCEPT_ENCODING", sizeof("HTTP_ACCEPT_ENCODING") - 1))) {
			convert_to_string(enc);
			if (strstr(Z_STRVAL_P(enc), "gzip")) {
				ZLIBG(compression_coding) = PHP_ZLIB_ENCODING_GZIP;
			} else if (strstr(Z_STRVAL_P(enc), "deflate")) {
				ZLIBG(compression_coding) = PHP_ZLIB_ENCODING_DEFLATE;
			}
		}
	}
	return ZLIBG(compression_coding);
}
/* }}} */

/* {{{ php_zlib_output_compression_start */
static void php_zlib_output_compression_start(void)
{
	zval zoh;
	php_output_handler *h;

	switch (ZLIBG(output_compression)) {
		case 0:
			break;
		case 1:
			ZLIBG(output_compression) = PHP_OUTPUT_HANDLER_DEFAULT_SIZE;
			ZEND_FALLTHROUGH;
		default:
			if (
				php_zlib_output_encoding() &&
				(h = php_zlib_output_handler_init(ZEND_STRL(PHP_ZLIB_OUTPUT_HANDLER_NAME), ZLIBG(output_compression), PHP_OUTPUT_HANDLER_STDFLAGS)) &&
				(SUCCESS == php_output_handler_start(h))
			) {
				if (ZLIBG(output_handler) && *ZLIBG(output_handler)) {
					ZVAL_STRING(&zoh, ZLIBG(output_handler));
					php_output_start_user(&zoh, ZLIBG(output_compression), PHP_OUTPUT_HANDLER_STDFLAGS);
					zval_ptr_dtor(&zoh);
				}
			}
			break;
	}
}
/* }}} */

/* {{{ PHP_RINIT_FUNCTION */
static PHP_RINIT_FUNCTION(zlib)
{
	ZLIBG(compression_coding) = 0;
	if (!ZLIBG(handler_registered)) {
		ZLIBG(output_compression) = ZLIBG(output_compression_default);
		php_zlib_output_compression_start();
	}

	return SUCCESS;
}
/* }}} */
